  "liner": {
   "body_md": "Mountain Goats played a duo show at the Hi-Dive in Denver on October 29, 2016, featuring John and Peter [1][2]. The recommended recording, captured by LMGBTapes, is the most complete option with 34 songs over 75 minutes [1]. This setlist includes rare archival moments, such as the only archived performance of \"John Is Sick\" and \"John Has Great Hair And Loves Get Lonely\" [1]. Listeners can also hear \"Spilling Towards Alpha,\" a bustout after 146 shows, and \"Moon Over Goldsboro,\" which returned after 96 performances [1]. The band played tracks from albums like *The Hound Chronicles*, *Get Lonely*, and *The Sunset Tree* [1]. A second recording by Lance Stack provides a 21-song matrix mix, but the primary file is preferred for its completeness [1][2]. The show featured banter, including John’s humorous stories about the Holiday Inn Express and his decision to stop playing \"Going to Georgia\" [1]. The encore included a unique bit where John and Peter hid behind stage objects before reappearing [1]. This recording captures the intimate energy of the performance, offering a rich snapshot of their live repertoire [2].",
